@anchor{jacobi_am}
@deffn {Function} jacobi_am (@var{u}, @var{m})
The Jacobi amplitude function, @mref{jacobi_am}, is defined implicitly by (see
@url{http://functions.wolfram.com/09.24.02.0001.01})
@html
\(z = {\rm am}(w, m)\)
@end html
@ifinfo
@math{z = am(w, m)}
@end ifinfo
@iftex
@math{z = {\rm am}(w, m)}
@end iftex
where @math{w = F(z,m)} where @math{F(z,m)} is the incomplete elliptic
integral of the first kind (@pxref{elliptic_f}).  It is defined for
all real and complex values of @math{z} and @math{m}.  In particular
for real @math{z} and @math{m} with @math{|m|<1},
@html
\({\rm am}(z,m)\)
@end html
@ifinfo
@math{am(z,m)}
@end ifinfo
@iftex
@math{{\rm am}(z,m)}
@end iftex
maps the entire real line to the entire real line.  For other values
of @math{z} and @math{m}, the following relationship is used:
@html
\({\rm am}(z,m) = \sin^{-1}({\rm jacobi\_sn}(z, m)).\)
@end html
@ifinfo
@math{am(z,m) = asin(jacobi_sn(z,m)).}
@end ifinfo
@iftex
@math{{\rm am}(z,m) = \sin^{-1}({\rm jacobi\_sn}(z, m)).}
@end iftex

Some examples:
@c ===beg===
@c jacobi_am(z,0);
@c jacobi_am(z,1);
@c jacobi_am(0,m);
@c jacobi_am(100, .5);
@c jacobi_am(0.5, 1.5);
@c jacobi_am(1.5b0, 1.5b0+%i);
@c ===end===
@example maxima
@group
(%i1) jacobi_am(z,0);
(%o1)                           z
@end group
@group
(%i2) jacobi_am(z,1);
                                 z    %pi
(%o2)                   2 atan(%e ) - ---
                                       2
@end group
@group
(%i3) jacobi_am(0,m);
(%o3)                           0
@end group
@group
(%i4) jacobi_am(100, .5);
(%o4)                   84.70311272411382
@end group
@group
(%i5) jacobi_am(0.5, 1.5);
(%o5)                  0.4707197897046991
@end group
@group
(%i6) jacobi_am(1.5b0, 1.5b0+%i);
(%o6)    9.340542168700782b-1 - 3.723960452146071b-1 %i
@end group
@end example

@c ===beg===
@c plot2d([jacobi_am(x,.4),jacobi_am(x,.7),jacobi_am(x,.99),jacobi_am(x,.999999)],[x,0,10*%pi]);
@c ===end===
@example maxima
@group
(%i1) plot2d([jacobi_am(x,.4),jacobi_am(x,.7),jacobi_am(x,.99),jacobi_am(x,.999999)],[x,0,10*%pi]);
(%o1)                         false
@end group
@end example

